# fzf's default options, read by fzf itself at every launch through FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS_FILE,
# which the zsh package exports and the tmux config sets in the server's environment. One
# file rather than a string in each, because the string used to live in both and drift
# between them, and because fzf reads a variable once per process where it reads this file
# every time it starts. That reaches a picker inside the tmux or herdr server, which froze
# its environment when it started, without restarting either.
#
# Every colour is an ANSI slot so it tracks whatever palette the terminal paints, which
# Ghostty paints from theme/ at the repository root. fzf's own defaults reach into xterm-256
# indexes like 108 and 151 that no theme repaints, so each one is routed through a slot here.
#
# info and header are text and read slot 4, the primary accent. They used to sit on slot 8
# with the lines, which stopped working when slot 8 became Aura's comment grey, quiet at 3.54
# to 1 on purpose. Slot 8 is the only neutral among the sixteen that works on both halves at
# all, since 7 and 15 collapse against a light page and 0 against a dark one, so the answer
# was an accent rather than a grey, which is what Catppuccin's own fzf theme does too.
#
# footer is slot 17, which Ghostty's theme-map declares as the overlay role, the grey of the
# secondary line in herdr's panel, so the key hints under a picker read like the line under a
# space rather than like a heading. It needs naming on its own because it does not follow
# header, it has its own default of cube index 109, a pale blue green no theme repaints,
# measured by drawing both lines and reading the escapes back. The prompt, the pointer and the
# matched text read slot 2, Aura's green, which fzf's own defaults approximate with cube
# indexes 108 and 151 that no theme repaints either, so a pale green in any of those three
# means this file is not being read.
#
# The bar under the current row is slot 16, which Ghostty's theme-map declares per half, the
# grey of herdr's focused row on light and the purple of its navigate row on dark. A bar has
# to be a tint of the page and no slot among the sixteen is dark on one half and light on the
# other, which is why it used to be a hex resolved inside one popup at draw time and every
# other fzf drew no bar. --highlight-line runs the tint across the whole row rather than under
# the text alone.
#
# The gutter is a glyph on every ordinary row, ▌ since fzf 0.6x, painted in the gutter colour
# as a foreground, so -1 left it in the ink, a dark bar on the light page and a light one on
# the dark page. It reads slot 18, which Ghostty's theme-map declares as dim, the quiet rule
# herdr's own borders take, so the column sits back the way a border does.
#
# border, separator and scrollbar stay on slot 8. They are lines rather than text and a quiet
# grey is what they want.
--color=fg:-1,bg:-1,fg+:-1,bg+:16
--color=hl:2,hl+:10
--color=prompt:2,pointer:2,marker:3,spinner:3
--color=info:4,header:4,footer:17
--color=border:8,separator:8,scrollbar:8,gutter:18
--highlight-line
